Hi Linxuan Ma,

No you're not being pedantic - good questions to ask. It is good to pre-download the DEMs when you're doing a lot of sites. I do it as pasted below - see if it works. Definitely don't let ERR go much above 3 - it is the error in the energy balance for the soil. It is probably because of very sudden changes in environmental conditions to do with your tide simulations.

All the best,
Mike

        dem.file <- paste0('dem/dem_', longlat[1], '_', longlat[2],'.tif')
        if(file.exists(dem.file)){
          dem <- terra::rast(dem.file)
        }else{
          dem <- NULL
          attempt <- 0
          while( is.null(dem) && attempt <= 10 ) {
            attempt <- attempt + 1
            try(
              dem <- microclima::get_dem(lat = longlat[2], long = longlat[1], resolution = 30, xdims = 100, ydims = 100) # mercator equal area projection
            )
          }
          #save(dem, file = paste0('dem/dem_', longlat[1], '_', longlat[2],'.Rda'))
          terra::writeRaster(dem, filename = dem.file, overwrite = TRUE)
        }

